      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The numeric datatypes that do not work are: byte, sbyte, short, and ushort.\nThe reason seems to be that VRChat is converting them to 32 bit ints.\nulong also no longer works, when it worked about a year ago.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-02-02T19:44:40.495Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In current version, it is not possible to properly sync Shorts and bytes. They are on the supported primitive sync list in documentation, but in practice they error out because internally they are cast to ints.\nThere are possibly other datatypes affected, I only note the two I tested",
